  "solution": {
    "text": "Normal molecular weight of acid can be found as<br /><br />Meq of acid = Meq of NaOH<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.75</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi>acid</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>;</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi>acid</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>250</mn></math><br /><br />Observed molecular weight of acid can be formed as<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi>acid</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi>acid</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>1000</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi>solvent</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.1</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.86</mo><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>250</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>1000</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://